    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultŭōsus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volt-</span></b> ), a, um,
			adj.
		vultus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of an expressive countenance</i>, <i>full of expression</i>, <i>full of airs</i> or
				<i>grimaces</i>, <i>grimacing</i>,
				<i>affected</i>: homo, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 171: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">frons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 3, p. 135, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne quid ineptum aut vultuosum sit (in
					oratione),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Or. 18, 60</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pronuntiatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 3, 183</span></i>
			.</div>
